{
    "_comment": "Phase 1.6 A4.5 (500-clip × ~2000-step data-scale clean eval). A4 was Weak PASS — held_out had driving structure but GT alignment weak + temporal jump + train_seen also not stably bound to clip. A4.5 isolates 'is the bottleneck data-scale or something else?' by 5× more clips, fixed-per-slot preview seed (clean evolution comparison), and stratified train_seen previews (4 different train scenes, not all from scene 0 like A4).",
    "_data": "500 train clips [0..499] (covers 17 nuScenes scenes, balanced 25-36 clips/scene per scripts/phase16_a4_scene_check.py extension). Train_seen preview indices [0,25,50,76] = 4 DIFFERENT train scenes (not all clip-0-of-same-scene like A4). Held_out [500,535,563,592,620,652,690,723] = 8 DIFFERENT scenes, all DISJOINT from the 17 train scenes (verified). PIN srun --nodelist=n3001-002.",
    "_dtype_strategy": "fp32 base / bf16 FSDP compute / fp32 reduce / no grad_scaler. WHY: ctsd.py:866-868 does `model.to(dtype=self.model_dtype)` BEFORE FSDP wrap, so writing model_dtype=fp16 means FSDP's 'sharded params kept in full precision outside fwd/bwd' would actually be fp16 — not real fp32 master. Omit model_dtype → defaults to fp32 → FSDP master is real fp32. Then mixed_precision.param_dtype=bf16 (compute), reduce_dtype=fp32 (gradient allreduce precision), buffer_dtype=fp32. autocast also bf16 (default cuda autocast = fp16 — must match FSDP compute dtype). enable_grad_scaler=false (bf16 doesn't need it). Matches PyTorch FSDP2 tutorial canonical pattern.",
    "_preview_indices_note": "validation/preview pool [0,25,50,76, 500,535,563,592,620,652,690,723]: 4 train_seen + 8 held_out_scenes, total 12 = 3 × WORLD_SIZE (4) → no DDP truncation. preview_dataloader cycle len 12 in slot order. preview-steps=170 → ~12 previews over 2000 steps (~one full cycle). Per-slot deterministic seed via inference_config.preview_seed_base — visual differences across cycles = pure model evolution, not generator drift.",
    "_mesh_note": "mesh_shape=[4] (1D, single node × 4 GPUs). PyTorch FSDP1 docs: 'FULL_SHARD = 1D mesh; HYBRID_SHARD = 2D mesh'. Earlier [1,4] caused FSDP to take the OUTER dim (size 1) → world_size=1 → silent fallback to NO_SHARD → fp16 model + grad_scaler → NaN. Confirmed via PyTorch FSDP API doc (https://docs.pytorch.org/docs/stable/fsdp.html).",
    "device": "cuda",
    "ddp_backend": "nccl",
    "_train_epochs_note": "500 clips / 4 ranks = 125 batches/rank/epoch (DistributedSampler shards). train_epochs=16 → 16×125=2000 global_step per rank (effective batch=4 → 8000 sample-views; ~16 exposures/clip vs A4's 40 — by design, A4.5 prioritizes diversity over per-clip overfit). Init from df16 NOT A4 1000.pth (avoid 100-clip prior bias polluting scaling judgment).",
